WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.200
Adding the source is half the case.

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.340
What happens if you take it away?

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.330
In the mouse, gene targeting can remove one gene.

4
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.410
The change is made in embryonic stem cells.

5
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.500
Wnt1 is made in a ring just in front of the line.

6
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.960
Mice lacking it lose most of the midbrain and much of the cerebellum.

7
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:27.863
Predict. In these mice, does Engrailed never come on?

8
00:00:28.643 --> 00:00:30.063
Or does it come on, and then fade?

9
00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:37.837
Engrailed comes on.

10
00:00:38.697 --> 00:00:40.717
Then it is lost, and the tissue disappears.

11
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:44.937
Wnt1 is needed to keep Engrailed on, not to turn it on.

12
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:48.027
Call this signature started, then lost.

13
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.430
So supplying Engrailed should help.

14
00:00:55.290 --> 00:01:01.750
In 1996, Danielian and McMahon made En1 from Wnt1's own control elements, in the

15
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.230
mutants. Early development of the region was restored.

16
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:08.763
A signal keeps a transcription factor on.

17
00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:11.583
The transcription factor keeps the territory.

18
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:15.047
FGF8 gives the same signature.

19
00:01:15.927 --> 00:01:21.247
In acerebellar, a zebrafish FGF8 mutant, boundary genes switch on, and then fade.

20
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.380
Mice that lose FGF8 early from the region lack midbrain and cerebellum.

21
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.940
Milder reductions spare part of both.

22
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:36.670
In these two mutants, the program does not fail to start.

23
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.550
It fails to last.

24
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:42.283
So the signals are needed to keep the program running.

25
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:47.783
In the standard model, built on other experiments too, the transcription factors

26
00:01:47.783 --> 00:01:49.063
help keep the signals on.

27
00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.683
Remove a key part, and the rest fade.

28
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:54.877
So the source has been tested three ways.

29
00:01:55.777 --> 00:01:57.257
Move it, add it, and take it away.

30
00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.430
Takeaway: a line becomes a source.

31
00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.170
It must stay on long enough for each part.

32
00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.570
Remove it too early, and parts are lost or changed.
